OL,3,GNEWSATrust warns of 'tangible' climate
OL,4,Athreat to heritage sites
OL,5,
OL,6,FProtecting all heritage sites from the
OL,7,Fimpact of climate change "just may not
OL,8,Fbe possible," according to a National
OL,9,FTrust manager.
OL,11,FJustin Scully, manager of Fountains
OL,12,FAbbey and Studley Royal, said extreme
OL,13,Fheat, heavy rainfall and wildfire risk
OL,14,Fwere already affecting gardens,
OL,15,Fmoorland and historic structures.
OL,17,FHe said heavy rain could overwhelm
OL,18,Fdrainage systems and penetrate walls,
OL,19,Fcausing damp and erosion, while
OL,20,Frepeated cycles of wetting, drying,
OL,21,Ffreezing and thawing could harm
OL,22,Fstonework.
OL,23,APub: 04-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,388,380,200,160,0,100
